From: Marco Martins
Subject: b43: drop a frame for the DTIM when its ring is full

Frames for stations in power save wait in the multicast ring for the
DTIM. When the ring was full, b43 stopped the mac80211 queue of the
frame that filled it, best effort for most broadcasts, and with it all
of that queue's traffic until the DTIM, a repeater's uplink's too. If no
DTIM comes, as when no beacons go out, the queue stays stopped, and
mac80211 holds every broadcast for it, with no bound: on the device the
held frames grew by about 2 a second, and the uplink stopped answering.

Drop such a frame instead, as mac80211 does when it buffers these frames
itself, and stop no queue for the multicast ring.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/dma.c
@@ -1348,6 +1348,15 @@
 	if (info->flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_SEND_AFTER_DTIM) {
 		/* The multicast ring will be sent after the DTIM */
 		ring = dev->dma.tx_ring_mcast;
+		/* A full ring waits for the DTIM, or for ever if none
+		 * comes: drop the frame rather than stop the queue, which
+		 * would stop all of its traffic and leave mac80211 holding
+		 * every frame for it. mac80211 drops them too when it
+		 * buffers them itself. */
+		if (free_slots(ring) < TX_SLOTS_PER_FRAME) {
+			ieee80211_free_txskb(dev->wl->hw, skb);
+			return 0;
+		}
 		/* Set the more-data bit. Ucode will clear it on
 		 * the last frame for us. */
 		hdr->frame_control |= cpu_to_le16(IEEE80211_FCTL_MOREDATA);
@@ -1395,8 +1404,9 @@
 		b43err(dev->wl, "DMA tx mapping failure\n");
 		goto out;
 	}
-	if ((free_slots(ring) < TX_SLOTS_PER_FRAME) ||
-	    should_inject_overflow(ring)) {
+	if (ring != dev->dma.tx_ring_mcast &&
+	    ((free_slots(ring) < TX_SLOTS_PER_FRAME) ||
+	     should_inject_overflow(ring))) {
 		/* This TX ring is full. */
 		unsigned int skb_mapping = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb);
 		b43_stop_queue(dev, skb_mapping);
